Keeps a profile's session cookies when its last window closes, as Chrome does only where the browser
lives on without windows (the Mac). Elsewhere it deletes them unless the profile's startup setting
restores the last session, which ilo never sets, though it always brings its tabs back and keeps
what they were signed in with (#1934). Closing the last window on Windows quits ilo, but its
browser window closes before the quit starts, so a sign-in kept in a session cookie went (#1998).

--- a/chrome/browser/sessions/session_data_service.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/sessions/session_data_service.cc
@@ -135,7 +135,9 @@
 
   // Session cookies should stay alive on platforms where the browser stays
   // alive without windows.
-  bool skip_session_cookies = browser_defaults::kBrowserAliveWithNoWindows;
+  // browser_core: and everywhere, as ilo brings its tabs back at every launch
+  // and keeps what they were signed in with.
+  bool skip_session_cookies = true;
 
   // Clear session data if the last window for a profile has been closed.
   StartCleanupInternal(skip_session_cookies);
